### ============================================================
### BFF: Search — the header search across all four kinds
###
### Read-only, no auth. `q` (at least 2 characters) runs each
### kind's own name search; `limit` (1–20, default 5) caps each
### group. Events are upcoming only; `past=true` adds the
### events that are over, latest first. Not response-cached.
### ============================================================

### Search everything for a venue name
GET {{bff-host}}/api/search?q=berghain
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
    });
    client.test("one group per kind", function () {
        ["events", "venues", "artists", "promoters"].forEach(function (kind) {
            client.assert(Array.isArray(response.body[kind].items), "Missing group " + kind);
        });
    });
%}

### Folded and typo-tolerant: finds ÆDEN and Berghain
GET {{bff-host}}/api/search?q=berghian&limit=3
Accept: application/json

### Past events too, as the results page asks
GET {{bff-host}}/api/search?q=berghain&limit=20&past=true
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("past events come back in their own group", function () {
        client.assert(Array.isArray(response.body.past.items), "Missing group past");
    });
%}

### A one-character term is a 400
GET {{bff-host}}/api/search?q=b
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 400", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "Expected 400");
    });
%}
